#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# elliptic_exp

#% text
# `elliptic_exp(u, [a, b])` gives the point `[x, y]` of the curve `y^2 = x^3 + a x^2 + b x` whose elliptic logarithm is `u`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `x = weierstrass_p(u) - a/3`, `y = weierstrass_p_prime(u)/2` for the invariants `g2 = 4 a^2/3 - 4 b`, `g3 = 4 a b/3 - 8 a^3/27`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
elliptic_exp(0.7, [1, 2])
#% output
#= [1.568359238723177, -3.074775100244476]

#% cell
n(elliptic_exp(1/2, [1, 2]), 30)
#% output
#= [3.58917180413188070041957268993, -8.1422823962940940151738367853]

#% cell
elliptic_exp(elliptic_log([2, 5], [3, 2.5]), [3, 2.5])
#% output
#= [2.0000000000000004, 5.000000000000001]

#% text
# Back to the logarithm:

#% cell
elliptic_log(elliptic_exp(0.7 + 0.2*im, [1, 2]), [1, 2])
#% output
#= 0.7 + 0.2im

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `elliptic_log`, `weierstrass_p`
